Jepy Dewan, a Senior Assistant Secretary at the Ministry of Water Resources in Bangladesh, reached out to Professor James Rising regarding potential PhD supervision, highlighting his background in circular economy, labor policy, and sustainable development. He expressed interest in climate policy and water management. James responded that he is not currently accepting PhD students but suggested Jepy consider master's programs in Environmental Economics or Environmental Science & Management at UD, noting that these programs are self-funded. He provided a link for more information and wished Jepy success in finding the right program.
